    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **271 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on the owner response, formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema (under the `allOf` object, alongside `id` and `pets`). Since the DTOs (`OwnerDto`) are generated at build time by the openapi-generator plugin, this is the correct place to introduce the field \u2014 it lands on `OwnerDto` but not on the input `OwnerFieldsDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct expression mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`. This automatically applies everywhere an `Owner` is mapped to `OwnerDto` (single owner responses, collections, and the V2 page listing).\n\n3. **`src/test/java/.../v1/OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 Extended `createOwnerSuccess` to assert `$.displayName` equals `\"Washington, George\"`.\n\nThe field is populated by the mapper, so it's returned on owner creation (POST `/api/owners`) exactly as specified, and consistently on all other owner responses too.",
